    /** Shape $ (Value): object. Shape $.object (Required): object and {@see InvoiceInput}. A bill issued to a customer. Shape $.object.cc_emails (Required): Array of string. Additional recipients copied on the invoice email and every reminder. Shape $.object.cc_emails[] (Value): string. Shape $.object.closed_at (Optional): string. When the current closed interval began. Cleared when status returns to open or partially_paid. A direct move between closed statuses preserves this timestamp. Format: date-time. Shape $.object.collection (Required): {@see InvoiceCollectionInput}. How this invoice is collected, resolved when the draft is written. Send this object back when updating its collection policy. The invoice collection policy resolved at write time. The object can be sent back when updating a draft. Shape $.object.collection_block_status (Required): string. Whether collection is blocked. While it is inventory_blocked, collection attempts return INVOICE_COLLECTION_BLOCKED. Value enum: "none", "inventory_blocked", "resolved". Shape $.object.created_at (Optional): string. When the invoice was created. Format: date-time. Shape $.object.credit_money (Required): {@see MoneyValueInput}. Credit note credit allocated to this invoice, minus reversed allocations. Unallocated credit isn't included. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. Shape $.object.currently_due_money (Required): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The part of the balance due now. Without schedule_entries, it equals outstanding_money. With schedule_entries, it is the outstanding amount of the first entry, in schedule order, whose due time has arrived and that still has a balance, or 0 when there is none. It is the amount the next collect call or checkout session charges. To total everything past due, add the outstanding_money of the entries whose status is due or overdue. Always 0 unless the invoice is open or partially_paid. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. Shape $.object.customer (Optional): {@see ExpandedCustomerSummaryInput} or null. Summary of the billed customer. Returned only with expand=customer. Shape $.object.customer.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedCustomerSummaryInput}. A customer's summary fields, returned in place of a customer ID when the customer is expanded. Shape $.object.customer.anyOf[2] (Value): null. Shape $.object.customer_id (Optional): string. Customer billed by this invoice. Absent when the invoice has no customer. Shape $.object.delivery_mode (Optional): string. How issue delivered the invoice. Value enum: "email", "caller_managed". Shape $.object.due_at (Optional): string. When payment is due. With payment terms, issue sets it from issued_at and the terms, counted in the invoice's timezone. Absent when the invoice has no due date. Format: date-time. Shape $.object.external_reference_id (Required): string or null. Caller-owned identifier for this resource in an external system. Use it as your sync key: it isn't printed on the invoice. null when unset. minLength: 1. maxLength: 255. Shape $.object.footer (Required): string or null. Fine print at the bottom of the invoice and PDF. It cannot change after issue. null when unset. Shape $.object.invoice_id (Required): string. Flint invoice ID. Shape $.object.invoice_number (Optional): string. Sequential document number assigned when the invoice is issued. Numbering is per merchant, with test and live mode numbered independently. Shape $.object.is_overdue (Required): boolean. Whether the invoice is open or partially_paid and past due with a balance remaining. Without schedule_entries, due_at has passed and outstanding_money is above zero; with them, at least one entry is overdue. Computed when the invoice is read. Shape $.object.issued_at (Optional): string. When the invoice was issued. Absent on a draft. Format: date-time. Shape $.object.late_fee_money (Required): {@see MoneyValueInput}. Late fees assessed after issue