 (Optional): string. When the invoice most recently became paid. Cleared when status leaves paid and set again on a later paid transition. Format: date-time. Shape $.object.paid_money (Required): {@see MoneyValueInput}. Payments collected toward this invoice, online or as recorded manual payments, minus reversed payments, including payments toward late fees. Never below zero. Refunds don't reduce it; they are in refunded_money. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. Shape $.object.payment_due (Required): {@see InvoicePaymentDueInput}. The resolved due-date policy. Send this object back when updating the draft; payment_terms captures the term's current revision again. The invoice due-date policy resolved at write time. The object can be sent back when updating a draft. Shape $.object.payment_terms_snapshot (Optional): {@see InvoicePaymentTermsSnapshotInput}. The payment term captured on the draft, with its due date rule and late fee policy. Later changes to the payment term don't affect this invoice. The payment terms saved on an invoice: the term's name, version, due date calculation, and late fee policy. Shape $.object.po_number (Required): string or null. The buyer's purchase order number, printed on the invoice and PDF. It cannot change after issue. null when unset. Shape $.object.public_url (Optional): string. The hosted invoice link where the buyer views and pays the invoice. Present after issue on API reads, except a list filtered by idempotency_key; webhook payloads leave it out. regenerate-public-link replaces it. Anyone with the link can open the invoice, so treat it as a secret. Shape $.object.recipient_email (Required): string or null. Where Flint emails the invoice and its reminders. Email delivery requires it at issue. null when unset. Shape $.object.reference (Required): string or null. Your reference for the invoice, printed on the invoice and PDF. The buyer's purchase order number goes in po_number. It cannot change after issue. null when unset. Shape $.object.refund_status (Required): string. How much of the collected money has been refunded. It doesn't change status. Value enum: "none", "partially_refunded", "refunded". Shape $.object.refunded_money (Required): {@see MoneyValueInput}. Money refunded to the buyer after collection. Refunds don't reopen the balance; refund_status summarizes them. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. Shape $.object.reminders_paused (Required): boolean. Whether automatic reminders are paused. Set reminders_paused on PATCH /v1/invoices/{invoice_id} to change it. Shape $.object.reminders_paused_at (Optional): string. When automatic reminders were paused. Absent while reminders are active. Format: date-time. Shape $.object.remit_to_address (Optional): {@see AddressInput}. Where the buyer sends offline payments, shown on the invoice. Defaults to the invoice settings remit-to address. A postal address. Every address has country. Addresses Flint checked as complete (customer and saved addresses, merchant, location, invoice, order delivery destination, tax identity, fulfillment recipient and pickup addresses) always have line1 and city, and US ones always have state and postal_code. Delivery quote destinations, buyer locations and postal-code tax locations hold only what was provided, such as postal_code and country. Shape $.object.schedule_entries (Required): Array of {@see InvoiceScheduleEntryInput}. The payment schedule, in schedule order. Always [] when the invoice has no schedule and is collected in one balance. Shape $.object.schedule_entries[] (Value): {@see InvoiceScheduleEntryInput}. One payment on an invoice's payment schedule, such as a deposit, installment, or balance, with its due time, amounts, and status. Shape $.object.scheduled_issue_at (Required): string or null. When Flint will issue and deliver this draft. null when no issue is scheduled. Cleared when the draft is issued or voided, or when you send null. Format: date-time. Shape $.object.service_date (Required): string or null. The calendar date of the billed service, in YYYY-MM-DD format. The invoice and PDF print it as written, without timezone conversion. null when unset. Format: date. Shape $.object.snapshot (Optional): {@see InvoiceSnapshotInput}. The billing content of the invoice: line items, discounts, charges, tip, tax, and totals. A draft previews the backing order; issue freezes it, and later order changes don't reach an issued invoice. A frozen copy of an issued invoice's content, including line items, charges, discounts, tax identities, and pricing amounts. Shape $.object.status (Required): string. Current invoice status. paid and credited close the current balance and can reopen to open or partially_paid after a payment or credit allocation reversal; invoice.reopened reports that change. void and uncollectible are final. Refunds change refund_status without reopening the balance. Value enum: "draft", "open", "partially_paid", "paid", "void", "uncollectible", "credited". Shape $.object.subscription_id (Required): string or null. The subscription the backing order belongs to, copied when the draft is created and never changed. null when the order isn't part of a subscription. Shape $.object.timezone (Optional): string. IANA time zone for the invoice's calendar dates, such as due dates from payment terms and reminder and late fee day counts. At issue, an invoice without one takes the invoice settings timezone. Shape $.object.total_money (Required): {@see MoneyValueInput}. What the issued invoice bills, equal to snapshot.pricing_amounts.total_money. Fixed at issue; a draft previews the backing order total. Late fees are in late_fee_money. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. Shape $.object.uncollectible_at (Optional): string. When the invoice was marked uncollectible. Format: date-time. Shape $.object.updated_at (Optional): string. When the invoice last changed. Format: date-time. Shape $.object.version (Required): integer string. Current invoice version. Send this as expected_version when updating the draft. Use an integer string (decimal digits), not a floating-point number. Format: int64. minimum: 1. Shape $.object.viewed_at (Optional): string. When the buyer first opened the invoice through its hosted invoice link. Recorded on a best-effort basis. Format: date-time. Shape $.object.voided_at (Optional): string. When the invoice was voided. Format: date-time. Shape $.object.written_off_money (Required): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The balance written off when the invoice was marked uncollectible, including unpaid late fees. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code.
